# Paths where a mistake is expensive and does not announce itself.
#
# Deliberately NOT a blanket `* @merrickphan`. With two people on opposite
# schedules, requiring the maintainer on every routine PR means work sits
# waiting overnight for a rubber stamp, and rubber stamps are how review stops
# being review. These are the files where that tradeoff flips.

# Packaging. v0.3.76 shipped with the whole ML stack excluded — the app degraded
# to word-overlap ranking silently, no error, while every measurement described
# a code path nobody was executing. A green build proves nothing here.
/electron-builder.yml   @merrickphan
/scripts/               @merrickphan

# Release and quality gates. Each check in here exists because a release already
# went wrong that way; weakening one is not a refactor.
/.github/               @merrickphan
/.claude/               @merrickphan

# ship.mjs owns the version field, and dependency changes reach the installer.
/package.json           @merrickphan
/package-lock.json      @merrickphan

# Sessions, tokens, and the code that decides who is signed in.
/src/main/services/auth/ @merrickphan

# The written reasoning behind all of the above.
/AGENTS.md              @merrickphan
/CLAUDE.md              @merrickphan
